From f06c170056d299f65f70d69d187c9701ac3261b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rtlsdr-wwb-scanner <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:26:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] scanner-v6: restore tuner registers after an I2C retry or
 failed write, no retries when the dongle is gone

- A tuner transfer that needed a retry may have met a tuner that was just
  reset (supply dip): its registers are at power-on values while the shadow
  copy says otherwise, and redundant-write skipping would keep them wrong
  until the device is reopened. After such a transfer all registers
  0x05..0x22 are written again from the shadow copy (as r82xx_init does),
  a read is repeated, and the PLL lock bit is checked again.
- After a write that failed for good (shadow_dirty), the next tuner write
  rewrites all registers; when that goes through without a retry, skipping
  works again (before: only after reopening).
- LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE: no retries, later tuner transfers fail at once,
  the 'i2c wr failed' line is printed once. Errors other than PIPE are
  retried only if the RTL2832U still answers (repeater can be switched on);
  PIPE is retried exactly as in scanner-v5.
- rtlsdr_get_tuner_restores(): number of full register rewrites; each one
  also prints "r82xx: tuner registers restored (N since open)".
---
 include/rtl-sdr.h     |  12 ++++
 include/rtlsdr_i2c.h  |   4 ++
 include/tuner_r82xx.h |   6 ++
 src/librtlsdr.c       |  71 +++++++++++++++++---
 src/tuner_r82xx.c     | 153 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 5 files changed, 221 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/rtl-sdr.h b/include/rtl-sdr.h
index 6ba410e..4abb460 100644
--- a/include/rtl-sdr.h
+++ b/include/rtl-sdr.h
@@ -443,6 +443,18 @@ RTLSDR_API const char *rtlsdr_get_build_info(void);
  */
 RTLSDR_API int rtlsdr_get_i2c_stats(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint32_t *retries, uint32_t *failures);
 
+/*!
+ * scanner-v6: how many times all tuner registers were written again from
+ * the driver's copy since the device was opened: after a tuner transfer
+ * that needed a retry (the tuner may have been reset) or after an earlier
+ * write that failed. R820T/R828D only.
+ *
+ * \param dev the device handle given by rtlsdr_open()
+ * \param restores number of full register rewrites (may be NULL)
+ * \return 0 on success, -1 no device or not an R82xx tuner
+ */
+RTLSDR_API int rtlsdr_get_tuner_restores(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint32_t *restores);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
